ence_ids":["E004","E005","E006","E007","E008","E010","E011","E012","E013","E014"],"reason":"Contains restored reviewed evidence."},{"methodology_id":"7B.8","status":"partially_covered","evidence_ids":["E007","E011","E012"],"reason":"Contains restored reviewed evidence."},{"methodology_id":"7B.9","status":"partially_covered","evidence_ids":["E008","E009"],"reason":"Contains restored reviewed evidence."},{"methodology_id":"7B.10","status":"partially_covered","evidence_ids":["E004","E005","E006","E007","E008","E009","E010","E011","E012","E013","E014"],"reason":"Contains restored reviewed evidence."}],"unresolved_gaps":["No usable local structured evidence was available for all 1B lenses.","Local structured evidence gaps remained for 3B.3, 3B.7, 5B.2, 5B.7, 6B.7, 7B.1-7B.5, 7B.8-7B.9, 8B.1, and 8B.8; these are not treated as favorable or adverse evidence.","The supplied compact handoff did not include the complete parent local-prior artifact paths or hashes for every methodology ID.","Several evidence claims concern inherited institutions, state systems, or mixed external/domestic causes rather than a uniquely personal act by Khamenei."],"evidence":[{"id":"E004","claim":"The mission said at least 26 people had reportedly been sentenced to death in protest-related cases and seven men had already been executed following proceedings marred by allegations of fair-trial violations and torture-tainted confessions.","publisher":"United Nations Office at Geneva","date":"2023-07-05","type":"UN fact-finding mission update","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_year","attribution":"strongly attributable to the state","contrary":["The government’s pardon claim exists, but does not address the reported execution and due-process failures."]},{"id":"E005","claim":"Iran’s media and civil-society environment made it difficult to uncover corruption, because the state tightly controlled broadcasting, censored newspapers, and filtered much online content.","publisher":"Freedom House","date":"2023","type":"rights-monitoring country report","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_year_and_inherited_context","attribution":"strongly attributable to the state","contrary":["Some outside reporting still existed, but under severe pressure and risk."]},{"id":"E006","claim":"The Fact-Finding Mission said it had sent seven letters seeking a visit to Iran and had not received answers, showing refusal to cooperate with independent investigation.","publisher":"United Nations Office at Geneva","date":"2023-07-05","type":"UN fact-finding mission update","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_year","attribution":"strongly attributable to the state leadership","contrary":["The state reportedly met the lead officials appointed to the Special Committee, but not the mission’s broader access requests."]},{"id":"E007","claim":"Reuters reported that Khamenei told officials in 2019 to do whatever it takes to stop protests and warned that the Islamic Republic was in danger, a report later mirrored by other outlets.","publisher":"Reuters / Radio Farda","date":"2019-12-23","type":"news investigation / wire report","confidence":"medium","use":"final_evidence","period":"inherited_context","attribution":"moderate to strong, but source-dependent","contrary":["Iran denied the account and Reuters could not independently verify the meeting."]},{"id":"E008","claim":"Treasury said the IRGC Cooperative Foundation functioned as a slush fund, senior IRGC and intelligence officials coordinated protest suppression, and the structure remained tied to corruption, graft, and privileged access.","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","date":"2023-01-23","type":"official sanctions finding","confidence":"medium","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_year","attribution":"strongly tied to the ruler’s system and senior loyalist networks","contrary":["This is a sanctions action, not a neutral audit; however, its organizational details are specific."]},{"id":"E009","claim":"Treasury said Bonyad Mostazafan was an opaque conglomerate under the Supreme Leader’s orbit, that it was used to enrich the office and reward political allies, and that the Supreme Leader had authority over its central accounts and personally profited from its holdings.","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","date":"2020-11-18","type":"official sanctions finding","confidence":"medium","use":"final_evidence","period":"inherited_context","attribution":"strongly linked to the ruler’s circle, though not a judicial adjudication of personal gain","contrary":["Treasury is an adversarial source; the record should be treated as strong allegation plus institutional evidence."]},{"id":"E010","claim":"Authorities arrested dozens of journalists, including reporters covering the Amini protests, and intimidated Persian-language media workers and their families.","publisher":"Freedom House","date":"2023","type":"rights-monitoring country report","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_year","attribution":"strongly attributable to the state","contrary":["Some independent reporting persisted, but not safely or freely."]},{"id":"E011","claim":"State television aired confessions extracted under duress, newspapers were censored, and internet and media restrictions were used to suppress critical reporting.","publisher":"Freedom House","date":"2023","type":"rights-monitoring country report","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_year_and_inherited_pattern","attribution":"strongly attributable to the state","contrary":["Critical reporting still occurred outside state media, but under serious risk and restriction."]},{"id":"E012","claim":"The mission reported continued arrests and detentions of protesters and women and girls refusing forced-veiling rules, plus harassment of family members and harsh punishments after the protests.","publisher":"United Nations Office at Geneva","date":"2023-07-05","type":"UN fact-finding mission update","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_year","attribution":"strongly attributable to the state","contrary":["The state’s pardon claim is the main partial counterpoint, but it did not eliminate the ongoing repression described."]},{"id":"E013","claim":"The UN mission said no official disaggregated data had been made public on people arrested, charged, or convicted in connection with the protests, and that intimidation and reprisals continued unabated.","publisher":"United Nations Office at Geneva","date":"2023-07-05","type":"UN fact-finding mission update","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_year","attribution":"strongly attributable to the state security apparatus under Khamenei","contrary":["The government said 22,000 pardons had been issued, but without the supporting data the claim remained opaque."]},{"id":"E014","claim":"The supreme leader’s decisions appeared unchallenged in practice and the Assembly of Experts’ oversight was confidential and ineffective, making independent accountability weak.","publisher":"Freedom House","date":"2023","type":"rights-monitoring country report","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"inherited_context","attribution":"directly tied to Khamenei’s political order","contrary":["Formal oversight institutions existed, but the report says they did not meaningfully constrain him."]},{"id":"E049","claim":"The U.S. State Department reported that Iran’s human-rights situation worsened in 2023, including 798 executions, intensified dress-code enforcement, and large-scale protest detentions and rearrests.","publisher":"www.ecoi.net","date":"unknown_not_exposed_by_source","type":"unknown_not_recorded","confidence":"unknown_not_recorded","use":"final_evidence","period":"unknown_not_recorded","attribution":"unknown_not_recorded","contrary":[]},{"id":"E053","claim":"In 2023 Iran’s supreme leader remained the decisive center of state power, with constitutional authority over national policy, the armed forces, and senior appointments, while formal oversight existed but was weak in practice.","publisher":"www.cfr.org","date":"unknown_not_exposed_by_source","type":"unknown_not_recorded","confidence":"unknown_not_recorded","use":"final_evidence","period":"unknown_not_recorded","attribution":"unknown_not_recorded","contrary":[]}]}
