cates a serious accountability concern within a security institution politically empowered by the López Obrador administration, while the report does not prove that López Obrador personally ordered obstruction.","publisher":"Associated Press","date":"2023","type":"reputable international reporting","confidence":"medium","use":"final_evidence","period":"Target-period and broader administration-period evidence","attribution":"moderate; AMLO expanded military responsibilities, but specific obstruction is attributed to military actors","contrary":["The government and military may dispute the allegation; independent judicial findings and complete case files remain necessary."]},{"id":"E014","claim":"ASF audit materials concerning Segalmex documented material procurement irregularities and possible public-finance losses in an agency created and overseen during the López Obrador administration. The record establishes an administration-level corruption and control failure, not personal enrichment by López Obrador.","publisher":"Auditoría Superior de la Federación","date":"2024","type":"official supreme-audit report","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"Later audit of administration-period conduct; retrospective evidence relevant to 2023 accountability","attribution":"strong for agency oversight and political responsibility; weak for personal profit or criminal intent","contrary":["Audits identify irregularities and financial observations, but final criminal liability requires prosecutorial or judicial findings; officials may contest observations."]},{"id":"E015","claim":"During the first four years of López Obrador’s administration, complaints against government responses to information requests were 19% higher than during the comparable period of the previous administration; INAI lost quorum in April 2023 after Senate appointments remained incomplete and the president vetoed two approved nominees.","publisher":"EL PAÍS México","date":"2023-04-24","type":"in