iance or misconduct.","contrary":["OGE reporting is administrative oversight, not a complete investigation of presidential-family conflicts."]},{"id":"E016","claim":"PolitiFact reported that a Washington Post investigation found no evidence Joe Biden personally benefited from or knew details about CEFC transactions involving Hunter Biden.","publisher":"PolitiFact","date":"2023-05-16","type":"fact_check","confidence":"medium_high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_period","attribution":"Relevant to personal financial benefit and knowledge claims, though the underlying transactions largely predated 2023.","contrary":["House Republicans argued that family business relationships created an appearance of influence."]},{"id":"E017","claim":"An October 2023 AP-NORC poll found 35% of adults believed Biden had done something illegal, 33% believed he had acted unethically but not illegally, and 30% believed he had done nothing wrong; AP reported that no evidence had emerged proving Biden abused office or accepted bribes.","publisher":"Associated Press/NORC","date":"2023-10","type":"polling_report","confidence":"medium_high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_period","attribution":"Strong for public trust and perception; not evidence that alleged misconduct occurred.","contrary":["Partisan polarization substantially affected responses."]},{"id":"E018","claim":"By December 2023, House Republicans had not established that Joe Biden participated in his family’s business dealings, directly benefited from them, or used his public position to assist the companies.","publisher":"FactCheck.org","date":"2023-12-14","type":"fact_check","confidence":"medium_high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_period","attribution":"Directly addresses allegations of personal enrichment and misuse of office.","contrary":["House Republicans continued to allege influence-peddling and investigative interference."]},{"id":"E019","claim":"Attorney General Merrick Garland appointed David Weiss special counsel with authority to continue and independently direct the Hunter Biden investigation and decide whether and where to file charges.","publisher":"U.S. Department of Justice","date":"2023-08-11","type":"official_record","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_period","attribution":"Institutional attribution is strong; no evidence opened that Biden personally directed the appointment or investigation.","contrary":["IRS whistleblowers and House Republicans alleged earlier interference and preferential treatment."]},{"id":"E020","claim":"In January 2023, the FBI searched Biden’s Wilmington residence with his lawyers’ cooperation and found items containing documents with classified markings and handwritten notes.","publisher":"Associated Press","date":"2023-01-21","type":"media","confidence":"medium_high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target_period","attribution":"Strong for Biden’s possession and cooperation; intent and culpability are not established.","contrary":["Later DOJ special-counsel review concluded criminal charges were not warranted."]},{"id":"E072","claim":"The February 2024 Hur investigation examined classified documents associated with Biden and concluded that criminal charges were not warranted, while raising document-handling and evidentiary concerns.","publisher":"www.justice.gov","date":"unknown_not_exposed_by_source","type":"unknown_not_recorded","confidence":"unknown_not_recorded","use":"final_evidence","period":"unknown_not_recorded","attribution":"unknown_not_recorded","contrary":[]}]}
