rable scrutiny applied to Party leaders or that prevention systems worked."]},{"id":"E015","claim":"The Vạn Thịnh Phát case exposed corruption networks reaching senior government levels and was linked in reporting to the January 2023 resignations and the continuing anti-corruption campaign.","publisher":"Associated Press","date":"2024-01-01","type":"investigative international reporting","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"later-retrospective on target-period events","attribution":"moderate for the enforcement environment; weak for personal culpability.","contrary":["The case demonstrates prosecution as well as failure of prevention and oversight."]},{"id":"E016","claim":"Trọng publicly called for officials with integrity, ability, and commitment to the public interest and described ethical and political degradation as a central anti-corruption concern.","publisher":"Vietnam Government News","date":"2023-05-17","type":"official speech","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target-period","attribution":"high for rhetoric and stated program; low for realized personnel standards.","contrary":["Independent evidence of merit-based appointments and correction remains limited."]},{"id":"E017","claim":"President Nguyễn Xuân Phúc resigned after corruption scandals involving officials under his political responsibility, making him the highest-ranking casualty of the anti-corruption drive at that time.","publisher":"Associated Press","date":"2023-01-17","type":"international news reporting","confidence":"high","use":"final_evidence","period":"target-period","attribution":"moderate for campaign context; low for a personal order by Trọng.","contrary":["The record does not establish that Trọng personally selected or caused the resignation."]},{"id":"E018","claim":"The legislature approved President Nguyễn Xuân Phúc’s resignation amid a major anti-corruption campaign, showing that political responsibility reached the highest state office.","publishe